Formally, the powers advance by $(x + yi)\,(-1 + i) = (-x-y) + (x-y)i$, which is exactly the decoding step:

{{algorithm:1}}

## Encode any Gaussian integer yourself

Every Gaussian integer has a unique canonical string of $0$s and $1$s. Try it: enter coordinates and watch the encoder read off the forced parity digit, divide by $\beta$, and repeat.

