## Uniqueness: a one-bit fingerprint

Uniqueness rests on a single fact: the last digit of $z = a + b\,i$ is always $(a+b) \bmod 2$, because every higher power of $\beta$ contributes an even amount to $a + b$. This parity fingerprint forces the digits one at a time.

