## Existence and the five stubborn points

Existence would be trivial if the size (Gaussian norm) shrank at every step -- but it does not. The norm strictly decreases everywhere **except** at exactly five points $\{i, -i, -1, -2+i, -2-i\}$. An exhaustive scan pins them down:

